1. The exact error
Your Argo CD output says:
failed to discover server resources
for group version cert-manager.io/v1:

the server could not find the requested resource


It also identifies the missing resources:
cert-manager.io/Certificate
cert-manager.io/Issuer


The Wazuh chart is trying to create these certificate resources:
Resource	Purpose
wazuh-root-ca	Root certificate
wazuh-admin	Indexer administration certificate
wazuh-node	Indexer node certificate
wazuh-dashboard	Dashboard certificate
wazuh-filebeat	Filebeat certificate
wazuh-ca-issuer	Certificate authority issuer
wazuh-selfsigned-issuer	Self-signed certificate issuer

Kubernetes does not recognize these resource types because the cert-manager Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs) are missing.

This also explains why:
- The wazuh namespace exists.
- No Wazuh pods exist.
- No PVCs exist.
- No Wazuh events exist.
Argo CD failed before it could create the workloads.
2. Install cert-manager first
I recommend installing it as a separate platform component, managed independently from Wazuh.

The official cert-manager installation documentation supports Kubernetes manifests, Helm and GitOps deployment. 
cert-manager Documentation+2


For a quick installation, use the official release manifest.

Run:
kubectl apply -f https://github.com/cert-manager/cert-manager/releases/download/v1.21.3/cert-manager.yaml


This installs:
- cert-manager CRDs
- cert-manager controller
- cert-manager webhook
- cert-manager CA injector
Do not install cert-manager inside the Wazuh Helm chart. It is a cluster-wide dependency and should be installed exactly once. 
